# Parked interactions lock (do not regress)

Anthony parked **Scenario** (2026-10-04) the same way as **Game Modes**: hide author-facing picks this version; keep the engines for later.

`npm test` must stay green (`src/lib/parkedInteractions.test.ts`).

## Invariants (code, not comments)

- **Scenario is not an author pick.** It must not appear in Course Settings interaction chips, the Course structure type dropdown, or the marketing examples carousel.
- **Do not persist it.** `stripParkedInteractionTypes` in [`src/lib/parkedInteractions.ts`](src/lib/parkedInteractions.ts) removes `scenario` on load, save, and cache. `PARKED_INTERACTION_TYPES` includes `scenario`.
- **Do not generate it.** Outline/hydrate must not whitelist `scenario` or call `generateScenarioData`. Storyboard remap still converts a one-question "Scenario:" screen to a quiz with `scenarioText`.
- **Keep the engine.** `ScenarioEngine`, `types/scenario.ts`, `ScenarioBuilderPanel`, and player rendering of existing `type: 'scenario'` slides stay in the repo.

## Game Modes (already parked)

Same pattern: Games tab filtered out; `gameTemplateIds: []`; outline strips `game-template`. Do not re-enable either pick unless Anthony explicitly restarts it.

## How to change this

Change `PARKED_INTERACTION_TYPES` / the picker lists and add a failing test first. Do not put Scenario back on the Course Settings grid "just to try it."
